/*
userEnvProbe
------------

Controls **how** the IDE backend collects your local environment variables and
passes them into supporting tools and processes defined in `.devcontainer.json`.

Valid options (default = `loginInteractiveShell`):

  • none
    No variables are pulled from the host; only those defined in the
    container image or in `.devcontainer.json` are available.

  • interactiveShell
    Runs a non-login interactive shell (e.g. Bash reads `/etc/bash.bashrc`
    and `~/.bashrc`). Login-only files such as `~/.profile` are **not** read.

  • loginShell
    Runs a login (non-interactive) shell, loading files like
    `/etc/profile`, `~/.bash_profile`, `~/.bash_login`, or `~/.profile`.

  • loginInteractiveShell
    Runs an interactive **login** shell, so it sources *all* of the above
    files. This gives the most complete set of variables.

The actual shell is whatever the user’s default is (usually Bash).

---

**Check what was imported**

Inside the container, inspect a variable with:

  echo "$USERPATH"
*/

{
  "name": "1_8-spec_userEnvProbe",
  "image": "ubuntu:latest",
  "userEnvProbe": "loginInteractiveShell",
  "runArgs": ["--env", "USERPATH=${localEnv:PATH}"]
}